source:
  name: Skinnytaste
  author: Gina Homolka
  url: https://www.skinnytaste.com/air-fryer-roasted-cauliflower-tacos/
servings: 2
yield: 6%tacos
prep time: 10m
cook time: 15m
---

> **Pickle the onions a day ahead** — They need a night in the refrigerator. Short on time, raw sliced red onion works too.

= Pickled Red Onions

Put the @red onion{1}(peeled, sliced into rounds) in a #heat-safe bowl{} with the @bay leaves{2}.

In a #small saucepan{}, heat the @apple cider vinegar{1/2%cup}, @water{1/3%cup}, @cane sugar{1%tbsp}(or maple syrup), and @kosher salt{1%tsp} until the liquid boils and the sugar dissolves. Pour the hot liquid over the onions.

Let the onions cool, move them to a #glass jar{}, and refrigerate overnight.

> **Storing** — This makes more than the tacos need. The onions keep in the refrigerator for at least 2 weeks.

= Tacos

In a #medium bowl{}, toss the @cauliflower florets{4%cup} with the @olive oil{2%tbsp}, @Tajín{1/2%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1/2%tsp}, and @&kosher salt{1/2%tsp}.

Spray the #air fryer{} basket with oil and add the cauliflower. Cook at 400°F (200°C), shaking the basket halfway through, until browned and tender, ~cook{12-15%minutes}.

Divide the cauliflower among the @tortillas{6}(street taco size). Top with pickled red onions, the @./peruvian-green-sauce{6%tbsp}, @?sour cream{}, and @cilantro{}.

> **Swaps** — No air fryer: roast the cauliflower in a 400°F (200°C) oven for about 20 minutes. Chili powder can stand in for the Tajín, and store-bought salsa verde for the green sauce. Avocado or red cabbage are good additions.
